WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.855 --> 00:00:05.011
Line 3 has to stand in hall B before the summer shutdown ends.

2
00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:08.802
The plan is right, but you are the youngest consultant.

3
00:00:09.861 --> 00:00:11.661
Two people do not report to you.

4
00:00:12.357 --> 00:00:16.548
The buyer has to order the switchboard this week, or it arrives too late.

5
00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:19.931
The team lead has to free his crew for the move.

6
00:00:20.922 --> 00:00:22.106
How do you get their help?

7
00:00:22.858 --> 00:00:26.132
We follow this project through the four topics of the module.

8
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.414
The first topic is Influence without authority.

9
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.082
You cannot order the buyer around.

10
00:00:33.854 --> 00:00:34.748
What do you do then?

11
00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:38.528
The sponsor only lends you a little position power,

12
00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:41.001
and it wears thin each time you use it.

13
00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:44.418
Your numbers are right and you know the line.

14
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.512
That is expert power.

15
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.257
You keep your word, and people like working with you.

16
00:00:50.971 --> 00:00:52.260
That is referent power.

17
00:00:53.275 --> 00:00:55.725
For influence we use a stakeholder map.

18
00:00:57.038 --> 00:01:00.591
The second topic is Feedback and difficult conversations.

19
00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:04.857
The team lead walked away twice during the start of the shift.

20
00:01:05.891 --> 00:01:08.038
Talk about behaviour, not character.

21
00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:10.609
Say what a camera would have recorded.

22
00:01:11.329 --> 00:01:14.266
He walked away, and the crew did not get the plan.

23
00:01:15.288 --> 00:01:17.899
Do it soon and in private, with a question.

24
00:01:18.731 --> 00:01:19.695
What was going on?

25
00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:23.107
Line 4 had stopped, and he had to go there.

26
00:01:24.241 --> 00:01:27.225
For feedback we use SBI and feedforward.

27
00:01:28.589 --> 00:01:30.911
The third topic is Listening and coaching.

28
00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:34.662
The buyer thinks the switchboard is too expensive.

29
00:01:35.669 --> 00:01:39.558
Under pressure you want to defend yourself or fix it right away.

30
00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:42.983
Listen first, and let the silence work.

31
00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:47.668
Whoever attacks the project usually has a worry underneath.

32
00:01:48.381 --> 00:01:51.480
The buyer’s is his budget, which has already been cut.

33
00:01:52.516 --> 00:01:54.838
We use active listening and MORE PIES.

34
00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:59.049
The fourth topic is Leading teams and yourself.

35
00:01:59.774 --> 00:02:03.547
On Monday you tell the crew and the team lead how the move goes.

36
00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:06.703
A first impression forms fast.

37
00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.834
Know your numbers, sit at the table and drop the hedge.

38
00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:13.104
Do you feel like a fraud?

39
00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.618
Then you act on evidence, not on feeling.

40
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:20.936
We use an assertive statement and reframing for your nerves.

41
00:02:22.253 --> 00:02:23.135
It connects.

42
00:02:23.862 --> 00:02:27.310
You build your own influence, give feedback on behaviour,

43
00:02:27.473 --> 00:02:29.331
and listen for the worry behind it.

44
00:02:30.119 --> 00:02:32.151
Then you say clearly what you propose.

45
00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:37.097
The buyer orders the switchboard, now that his worry has been heard.

46
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:42.755
The team lead frees his crew, because his worry about line 4 has been heard too.

47
00:02:43.461 --> 00:02:45.377
Line 3 gets into place.

48
00:02:46.721 --> 00:02:48.393
This is the map of Projects.

49
00:02:49.128 --> 00:02:53.099
Leading people is the second station of People and influence.

50
00:02:54.168 --> 00:02:57.384
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

51
00:02:58.371 --> 00:03:01.773
Start with Influence without authority, at Basics level.

52
00:03:02.817 --> 00:03:06.903
At Working knowledge you add the stages of a team, the line to manipulation,

53
00:03:07.031 --> 00:03:09.190
Toyota Kata and Radical Candor.

54
00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:14.424
At Advanced you add trading with currency, the identity conversation,

55
00:03:14.575 --> 00:03:16.990
coaching cycles and team dynamics.

56
00:03:17.999 --> 00:03:21.355
At Expert you add coalitions, feedback that hits you,

57
00:03:21.436 --> 00:03:24.501
situational leadership and psychological safety.

58
00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.701
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
